course: dictionary
lesson: 9325
title: Spice: flavour and excitement
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning. Spice can name something you eat or add to food, and it can also mean excitement. The words around it show which meaning the writer wants. «Spices were dear in medieval Europe but not usually worth as much as gold.» Dear means expensive here, so spices must be costly things, not a lesson in friendship.
explain: Look at the little words too. To spice food means to add spices to it. To spice something up means to make it more exciting, and the word up is a clue that it means more, not that you add a flavour.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. Read «variety is the spice of life» and swap in excitement: variety is the excitement of life. It still makes sense, so spice here means something that stops life being boring.
explain: Keepers sometimes spray perfume or spices in an enclosure, because new smells give cats something to explore, like a new toy. The spices are used for their smell, not for dinner. The clue is the toy: new smells are interesting, so the sentence is about interest.
fact: A spice is a dried part of a plant, such as seeds, bark or roots, used to give food a strong flavour.
fact: Pepper, cinnamon, ginger and cumin are all spices.
fact: «Spice» can also mean excitement or interest that makes something less boring.
fact: To «spice something up» means to make it more exciting or interesting.
fact: Long ago, spices were carried along trade roads over long distances and were very valuable.
exercise: «Spices were dear in medieval Europe.» What does dear mean here? | Hot to touch | Very small | *Expensive | Cheap
exercise: «Variety is the spice of life.» In this sentence spice means: | *Excitement that stops life being boring | A pan for cooking | Pepper and ginger for dinner | A dried leaf for making tea
exercise: «The teacher wanted to spice up the lesson with a game.» What does spice up mean? | *Make it more exciting | Make it cheap | Make it shorter | Make it quiet
test: Which of these is a spice? | Apple | Bread | *Cinnamon | Milk
test: «Variety is the spice of life.» What does spice mean here? | A type of bread | A pan for cooking | A dried leaf for tea | *Something that adds interest and stops things being dull
exam: Ana says spice only means something you put in soup. Is she right? | *No, spice also means excitement that makes something less boring | Yes, spice only ever means food | Yes, but only in soup and nowhere else
